From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] iphlpapi, nsiproxy: IP interface table, and change notifications that call back

- GetIpInterfaceTable failed with ERROR_NOT_SUPPORTED, and
  GetIpInterfaceEntry and InitializeIpInterfaceEntry were missing. Each
  link gives an IPv4 row, and an IPv6 row when the host has IPv6: index,
  LUID, MTU, connected state, the automatic metric by link speed (75 for
  loopback), and Windows' defaults for the settings the host does not
  keep per family. InitializeIpInterfaceEntry marks every setting
  "unchanged".
- NotifyIpInterfaceChange and NotifyRouteChange2 never called back, and
  NotifyUnicastIpAddressChange gave only its initial notification. A
  registration now has a thread that waits for the NSI tables' change
  notifications, takes the table again and calls back with each instance
  added, deleted or changed (lifetimes counting down are not changes). The
  initial notification still comes before the call returns.
  CancelMibChangeNotify2 stops the thread, waiting for a callback in
  progress unless called from one.
- NotifyRouteChange failed: it waits for the IPv4 route table.
- NotifyStableUnicastIpAddressTable was missing: addresses are never left
  tentative here, so the table comes back at once.
- nsiproxy listens for link and route netlink messages too, and signals
  the NDIS interface and IP forward tables.

Wine's iphlpapi tests: GetIpInterfaceTable/GetIpInterfaceEntry test added;
no failures, as before.

Gate: test/ipnotify-gate.sh (a network namespace of its own; adds an
address, a route and a link). Mutants SG_MUTANT_NO_MIB_NOTIFY,
SG_MUTANT_NO_IP_INTERFACES (iphlpapi_main.c), SG_MUTANT_NO_LINK_ROUTE_EVENTS
(nsiproxy.sys/nsi.c).
